The vendored source was vendored by the arniko project to make the
widget available through the arniko umbrella's `tornado` crate under
the `sparkline` feature flag. The arniko project chose this vendoring
arrangement to keep the consumer contract small and to avoid taking a
direct path-dependency on the upstream `ratatui` crate for callers
that only need the `Sparkline` widget.

Modifications from upstream
---------------------------

The vendored source is verbatim from
`ratatui-v0.30.0/src/widgets/sparkline.rs`. No functionally-significant
changes were made. The source was vendored into a single-file
`src/lib.rs` for ease of vendoring; upstream's module split was not
realized in this vendoring because the upstream `Sparkline` source is
a single file with no internal submodules.

The upstream `Sparkline` widget has only a `Widget` impl. There is no
`StatefulWidget for Sparkline` and no `SparklineState` upstream; this
crate's public surface matches that contract.

Upstream import-path note
-------------------------

Upstream 0.30 imports ratatui via a single merged crate (the
unstable 0.29-era subcrate split `ratatui-widgets::widgets::*` was
reverted in 0.30). The vendored `src/lib.rs` therefore uses the
single-crate `use ratatui::widgets::Widget;` path. No path rewrite
was needed.

